Subject: [PATCH 2/3] jails/instances/lab-claude: Keep mbsync's state in each
 folder
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab@lists.p7x.dev
Change-Id: lpvkltvotmlwzuppprpkqqwtkwznlplt
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:37:43 +0000

mbsync keeps its sync state in ~/.local/state/isync by default, apart
from the folders it describes. Once the mail root is removed or made
again, that state no longer matches the folders, and every later sync
of the list fails with "Unable to recover from UIDVALIDITY change".
lab-claude has such state now, from a sync into a mail root that is
gone. lab-claude's copy is only a mirror of lab-mail, so starting over
should be as easy as removing the mail root.

notmuch already ignores mbsync's state files, so they are not indexed
as mail.
---
change-id: lpvkltvotmlwzuppprpkqqwtkwznlplt

 jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.mbsyncrc | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.mbsyncrc b/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.mbsyncrc
index f09acc0f..163f4e3c 100644
--- a/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.mbsyncrc
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-claude/dist/home/claude/.mbsyncrc
@@ -4,6 +4,10 @@
 # write it reads it with any password, so the password here is a
 # placeholder. claude@p7x.dev cannot change the list, so the sync
 # only pulls, and Expunge Near drops what has gone from lab-mail.
+#
+# SyncState * keeps each folder's sync state in the folder, so a mail
+# root that is removed takes its state with it, and the next sync
+# pulls the list afresh.
 
 IMAPAccount lab-mail
 Host 127.0.0.1
@@ -28,4 +32,5 @@ Create Near
 Sync Pull
 Expunge Near
 Remove None
+SyncState *
 CopyArrivalDate yes
